# Meridian — Provisional Action Plan
## Gendarme Graticule / Geometric Solver Symmetry Program

### Primary objective

Develop the **Gendarme Graticule** as an independent geometric solver and determine what structural information its intrinsic symmetries, asymmetries, degeneracies, and transformations actually generate.

In parallel, compare that structure with the existing **Universal Indicatrix (UI/TX), Whirligig, and Spheres** solvers so that we can later test whether any individual solver—or combinations among them—naturally reproduce meaningful categorical structures found in Standard Model physics or in SAT/H(s)H particle interpretations.

The immediate rule is:

> Derive the geometry first. Compare it with physics second. Do not tune the geometry to obtain a desired correspondence.

### A. Freeze the current Graticule primitives

Preserve the construction already discovered before adding new interpretation.

Current primitives include:

- embedded ring torus;
- major and minor circumferences;
- inner / outer distinction;
- primary-circumference tangent as the null reference;
- vector-angle pin with \(90^\circ\) as null trajectory;
- straight tangent versus torus-proper tangent;
- ordinary versus anti-graticule as exact inner↔outer mirror partners;
- CW / CCW traversal;
- prograde / retrograde relation;
- left / right handedness where independently defined;
- cross-sectional radial coordinate and angular position.

No two binary distinctions should be identified merely because they sometimes correlate.

### B. Reconstruct the metric ledger

Retain all discovered metrics rather than reducing prematurely.

Current families include:

- major-circumference scale;
- axial asymptopy;
- graded helical chirality;
- vector-angle / chiral-flip relation;
- winding / rotation-number relation;
- flicker / rational-irrational recurrence structure;
- separatrix / asymptotic transition;
- holonomy;
- reconnection / closure;
- radial or “macular” structure;
- ordinary / anti residuals.

