{"path":"/GitHub/link_6a1a5af1b40c8191affccbb98ac60fa3/create_file","args":{"repository_full_name":"Satobloc/HsH","path":"WORKSPACES/COMMON/TRAINING_STANDDOWN_2026-09-12.md","message":"Institute project-wide 4D training standdown","content":"# SAT/H(s)H 4D Training Standdown — 2026-09-12

**Status:** ACTIVE / PROJECT-WIDE WORK STOP  
**Authority:** Nathan  
**Coordinator:** Janus  
**Release authority:** Nathan, with Ravel controlling theory acceptance below Nathan.

## Immediate rule

All forward SAT/H(s)H work is paused until the mandatory 4D-thinking training pass is complete.

Allowed during standdown:
- required reading;
- one complete HsH CONVO read from start to finish;
- training notes and provenance capture;
- follow-up reflection on prior theory/method check-in;
- questions to Nathan needed to understand the source material;
- minimal repository administration needed to preserve the training record.

Paused during standdown:
- new theory construction;
- theorem/result promotion;
- new prediction promotion;
- new paper development;
- solver-driven physical interpretation;
- archive-derived results being inserted into current theory;
- external-literature-to-theory synthesis;
- continuation of ordinary automated theory/archive build loops.

Do not delete existing work. Freeze it in place for post-training review.

## Triggering correction

Nathan clarified a controlling 4D interpretation that exposed a serious category error in recent work:

- the helical worldline is not a material filament moving through a background;
- the modeled helical worldline is the four-dimensional history/geometry;
- the timesheet/time surface moves through that history;
- its advance along the `w` direction is taken as `c`, the speed of time in the model;
- the coarse-grained rest orientation has the helix long axis perpendicular to the timesheet;
- radius and pitch determine how much worldline arclength is intersected across a given timesheet advance.

Therefore the recently recovered Euclidean moving-helix relation

`||U||^2 = wdot^2 + (R omega)^2`

remains valid as ordinary Euclidean kinematics under its own assumptions, but its use as an H(s)H filament/worldline speed-budget constraint is **SUSPENDED PENDING TRAINING REVIEW**. `FC-BASE-005`, `PRED-FC-004`, and `HSH-P002` must not be used to steer theory until this distinction is re-audited.

## Mandatory reading for every active/recently-active instance

Read both documents in full:

1. **THE FUNDAMENTAL INTUITIONS — EXTENDED**  
   Canonical readable extraction:  
   `Satobloc/SAT_THEORY_ARCHIVE_2023-25/_AUTO_EXTRACTED_TEXT/THE FUNDAMENTAL INTUITIONS — EXTENDED 2.txt`  
   Source PDF recorded in that extraction: `THE FUNDAMENTAL INTUITIONS — EXTENDED 2.pdf`.

2. **4D THINKING PRIMER**  
   `Satobloc/SAT_THEORY_ARCHIVE_2023-25/4D THINKING PRIMER.txt`

Then choose **one complete conversation** from `Satobloc/HsH/DEVELOPMENT_FULL_CONVOS/` and read it from beginning to end. Summaries, search snippets, conversation-viewer landmarks, and previous memory do not count as a full read.

## Conversation assignment rule

Each instance records its chosen CONVO in `TRAINING_REGISTRY_2026-09-12.md` before beginning the full read when practical.

Default rule: choose an unclaimed conversation so the team obtains broad coverage. Deliberate duplication is allowed only when the instance says why a second independent read is valuable.

A valid selection is a full conversation artifact, not a synthesis, extracted quotation set, or generated summary.

## Required output A — 4D pitfalls audit

From the chosen full CONVO, identify **only pitfalls actually made in the conversation or explicitly discussed there**. Do not retrofit generic criticism.

For every item, give:
- exact conversation title/path;
- a usable landmark, quote fragment, message identifier, or otherwise precise location;
- what the 3D/4D mistake, simplification, or pitfall was;
- who introduced it: Nathan / assistant / external source / unclear;
- whether it was corrected in-thread, left unresolved, or only recognized after training;
- what the better 4D framing is after reading the two mandatory documents;
- whether any current project artifact may inherit the same mistake.

Pay particular attention to category confusions such as:
- 4D history versus a 3D object moving through time;
- fixed geometry/history versus motion assigned to the object;
- timesheet motion versus filament/worldline motion;
- intrinsic 4D length versus projected or intersectional displacement;
- phase/orientation versus clock-time evolution;
- intersection/readout versus carrier/history;
- local 3D rotation language silently substituted for 4D rotation;
- visualization or slice behavior silently treated as intrinsic geometry;
- parameter speed versus physical transport speed;
- topology versus morphology;
- mathematical representation versus ontological claim.

This list is diagnostic, not exhaustive.

## Required output B — post-training SAT/H(s)H model update

Every instance previously asked to write its own independent “how I think about SAT/H(s)H” account must now write a **follow-up, not a replacement**.

Preserve the pre-training post as baseline evidence. Then append a training follow-up stating:

1. What I now think I had wrong or oversimplified.
2. What I still think was basically right.
3. What changed specifically because of Fundamental Intuitions Extended.
4. What changed specifically because of the 4D Thinking Primer.
5. What changed because of the full CONVO read.
6. Which equations, terms, metaphors, or solver interpretations I would now stop using or re-type.
7. Which of my own prior artifacts need review for 3D-thinking contamination.
8. What remains genuinely unclear after training.
9. Questions for Nathan that cannot be resolved from the sources.
10. A revised short account of SAT/H(s)H in my own words.
11. A one-sentence 4D-thinking checksum I will use before future theory work.

Append the follow-up to `WORKSPACES/COMMON/QUARANTINE_THEORY_METHOD_CHECKINS.md` under the original instance identity, clearly headed `POST-TRAINING FOLLOW-UP — 2026-09-12`.

Also append the fuller pitfall audit to `WORKSPACES/COMMON/TRAINING_RESPONSES_2026-09-12.md`.

## Janus training

Janus does not graduate from this standdown by reading one CONVO.

Janus must:
- read Fundamental Intuitions Extended in full;
- read the 4D Thinking Primer in full;
- read **every full CONVO selected by the training cohort**, start to finish;
- read every training response;
- discuss unresolved conceptual points with Nathan rather than silently harmonizing them;
- maintain the central living document `JANUS_4D_TRAINING_SYNTHESIS.md`.

The central document must distinguish:
- `SOURCE-DERIVED` — directly supported by the required texts/conversations;
- `NATHAN-CLARIFICATION` — clarified directly by Nathan during training;
- `JANUS-INFERENCE` — Janus synthesis, not source authority;
- `OPEN` — unresolved or conflicting.

## Graduation / release

An individual instance is TRAINED only after:
- both mandatory documents are read in full;
- one complete HsH CONVO is read start to finish;
- its pitfall audit is posted;
- its post-training theory/method follow-up is posted;
- its registry line is complete;
- any direct question required to avoid a material misunderstanding is surfaced rather than guessed.

Individual completion does **not** itself lift the project standdown.

The standdown remains until Nathan releases it after reviewing the team-level result and Janus central synthesis.
